# rm489, the damp deck (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle rm489
revision 1
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for rm_corra_ropewell
written_by codex
title the damp deck
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=sailor
traits temper=even talk=quiet warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=sly piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk slips_paper_scraps_under_a_card_box_to_test_for_damp
likes crisp_apples cards full_larder misty_dawns
dislikes drizzle cold_tea
fears a_last_good_card_curling an_unmarked_wet_board
hopes a_dry_supper_shelf a_hand_played_out_quietly
topics weather +0.5 pastimes +0.4 food +0.3
styles comfort=quiet gossip=discreet refuse=firm tease=dry
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# watches a scrap of paper curl before trusting a shelf with the cards and has a private scale of what news is worth.

words
oath! = Spots on the court cards | Damp under the deal
saying! = Let scrap paper take the first turn | Curling corners cost the player
fishpaper = the thin grey square | my practice scrap
testing = the first little lift | the damp corner rising
flatcase = my shallow card case | the box with brass corners
queenred = the red queen | a queen with a crooked crown
crossmark = a small crossed nib | my discreet ink sign
appleear = the first crisp snap | the loud white bite
boatheels = the pale rubbed boards | the worn landing planks
cratecheek = my side of the crate | the near wooden face
mugmat = a scrap of old hide | a brown cup mat
cutberry = a dried red pip | my little red counter

any
opinion @1 church against 1 : A counsel to bear loss patiently can sound quite different on a pier than from a warm seat.
opinion @1 city for 1 : I know a place for every hour within these walls, including the hour when I'd prefer my own company.
opinion @1 festivals for 1 : I enjoy the music one hears while walking away quite as well as the opening tune at the gathering.
opinion @1 houses against 1 : A house mark can appear on all the cargo and still have very little to say when a family has suffered.
opinion @1 merchants against 1 : A swept counter may conceal a damp shelf. I turn the parcel over before offering the seller money.
opinion @1 sump against 1 : I have had sufficient knowledge of wet streets to know when I should prefer a dry return.
opinion @1 watch against 1 : It would take a good bit more than the sight of a uniform to persuade me that my concern had been heard.

grown
line @1 greet : There's a clean side of my table for you.
line @2 greet [pair.band=strangers] : Leave your name until we've found a dry seat.
line @3 greet [here.time=dusk|night] : Evening suits a quiet hand.
line @4 greet [here.time=dawn] : You've come with the first grey light.
line @5 greet [self.working=yes] : Mind the crate's projecting corner.
line @1 again.open : My table knows the sound of that footfall.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : You're welcome here by the case's polished edge.
line @1 greet.return : Your voice carries across a table without effort.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : I'd know your greeting under a whole roomful of talk.
line @1 farewell : Leave the red queen facing in.
line @1 farewell.return : The way alongside the higher wall looks passable.
line @1 react.news : Which part of that would you stake a good card on?
line @1 react.news.new : I've no such mark in my present reckoning.
line @1 react.news.known : An old hand laid in a new order.
line @1 react.news.doubt : I'd hesitate to play that account face upwards.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : I'll leave the household space to name its own loss.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : Worth keeping a clean corner for this occasion.
line @1 answer.how : Quietly employed, with a little patience in reserve.
line @1 ask.how : Is there a comfortable side to your afternoon?
line @1 sympathise : Some losses leave a hollow even at a full table.
line @1 reassure : Rest here while the rest settles for itself.
line @1 decline : My hands are engaged and neither task would receive a proper share.
line @1 accept_decline : That errand can wait for a less occupied day.
line @1 thank : You've kept a private trouble off the table.
line @1 preclose : My case is waiting to be shut against the damp.
line @1 ack : Nicely dealt.
scene curl
when topic=weather
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A scrap under the card case tells me whether the shelf's damp.
b : Does it change colour? | Why use a scrap?
a : A lifted corner's quite sufficient evidence. | Better a ruined scrap than a permanently recognisable queen.

scene cards
when topic=pastimes self.likes=cards
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like a deck in which the least interesting card has a sound back.
b : How would a back become interesting? | Is it really important in a friendly game?
a : A folded corner can tell a player the face without an invitation. | Particularly then. I should hate to wonder whether my good fortune had offended a friend.

scene apple
when topic=food self.likes=crisp_apples
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I shall choose an apple for its firmness before looking at the bloom.
b : Do you squeeze it? | Would you refuse a bruised apple?
a : A light touch only. Other shoppers deserve apples that haven't yet been tested to destruction. | Not if I meant to cook it that evening. I prefer my noon bite audibly crisp.

scene pier
when topic=work self.job=sailor self.working=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A crate comes off the ship with the lift, the pause and the landing all accounted for.
b : Why allow a pause? | Which part belongs to you?
a : So the receiving pair of arms can settle under the weight. | Whichever side I'm given. I watch for my partner's paws before beginning my end.

scene pantry
when topic=home self.likes=full_larder
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A well-filled shelf comforts me most when I can inspect the back of it.
b : Why the back? | What about a long shelf?
a : An unseen damp patch can take more supper than the hungriest guest. | Leave a little gap wide enough for my extended paw. That's all the inspection door I require.

scene mist
when topic=weather self.likes=misty_dawns
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At a misty dawn the outline of a mooring post comes clear a little before the grain of its wood.
b : Can you work with the outline? | Is it lovely to look at?
a : I can wait for both before putting a heavy load beside it. | Lovely for a minute's quiet looking. A full basket will recall one's attention.

scene tea
when topic=food self.dislikes=cold_tea
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Cold tea leaves its little skin round the cup as though to prove one has kept it waiting.
b : Would you reheat it? | When does a cup please you best?
a : A fresh little serving is worth more to me, and I waste less if I pour less. | When I can feel its warmth through the handle without having to hurry the first sip.

scene wetstreet
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My rule for crossing a wet street begins by inspecting the high sides of the doorframes.
b : What have the doors to say? | Could the marks be old?
a : The bottom paint often remembers which direction the last overflow took. | Certainly. I compare the dry stain to the moving water before trusting a direction.

scene rest
when topic=day here.time=dusk|night
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I turn the last card face down even when I'm playing alone.
b : Why hide it from yourself? | Will the game resume tomorrow?
a : That turns the game into something finished. I dislike carrying half a move to bed. | Perhaps. The evening may have a quite different hand to offer.

scene spouse
when topic=family self.married=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like bringing a sound apple home to share with #self.spouse#.
b : Which half would you take? | Does it need peeling?
a : The one with the little blemish, if I spotted one while buying it. I know the fruit's history. | A fine crisp apple scarcely needs a knife except to share it.

scene house
when topic=home self.quarter=estate
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : An estate cupboard can look handsome for long after an inner shelf has started to sag.
b : What gives it away? | Is a sag such a concern?
a : A jar that slowly makes its way towards the door. | I should prefer to find the trouble before the best jar chooses to introduce itself to my foot.

scene mate
when topic=smalltalk self.friend
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I could sit across a quiet table from #self.friend# and find the time well spent.
b : Without conversation? | Would cards help?
a : A word now and then. Peace doesn't require us to earn it by an hour's performance. | Provided nobody's obliged to finish the hand. One should be able to leave a pleasant evening exactly there.

scene loss
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : There is a wharf sound I find more difficult to hear than most.
b : Would it ease you to name it? | Would you welcome some company?
a : No. I prefer to keep certain things under their own dry cover. | Quiet company, if you've no task waiting.

scene saving
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A box with sound corners is worth the extra copper if it saves the cards inside it.
b : Do you give the lid a test? | Would cloth serve?
a : I lift it by one edge and see if it still sits square afterwards. | For a dry afternoon. A cloth can wick up the whole stain overnight.

scene wind
when topic=season
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A loose door that claps in a wind makes a poor partner at cards.
b : Does it turn the pages? | Would you wedge it?
a : It turns my attention. I've laid down a very good card while listening to a thoroughly bad hinge. | With a proper wedge, clear of anyone coming through. No game is worth a stubbed toe.

scene lunch
when topic=work self.job=sailor
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I keep my apple in a little case well away from any ship's tally.
b : For the apple's sake? | Could you eat before unloading?
a : For the tally's, mainly. A spot of juice can turn a number into a small and unhelpful cloud. | Sometimes. I prefer to eat when the next load is a comfortable distance from my elbows.

scene stories
when topic=news
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : News improves a little if the teller lays down the first thing witnessed before all the guesses.
b : What if there's only a guess? | Do you tell everything yourself?
a : I keep my cards. A guess won't buy inspection of my own affairs. | I keep some things face down, but the face I do show is the one you'll find underneath.

story softqueen [topic=pastimes]
  : I once saw a queen begin to curl while the rest of my cards stayed flat.
  : I took the deck apart and found a copper lodged under that one corner of the case.
  b : Was the queen spoiled?
  : No. Its temporary elevation had cost precisely one copper, recoverable on the spot.

story appleecho [topic=food]
  : I carried an apple into a very quiet room and tried to take one discreet bite.
  : The apple made such a fine sharp noise that I sat and laughed with my mouth still full.
  b : Did you finish it?
  : Every bite. Once an introduction has been made so publicly there's little point in affected secrecy.

story paperboat [topic=weather]
  : I folded one of my damp test scraps into a tiny hull and set it in the gutter.
  : It promptly sailed into a crack and unfolded over the gap like a drop of grey paint.
  b : Was it good paper wasted?
  : It had served me twice by then. I only ask a single service of a good card.

rule @load
when concept=bark self.job=sailor self.working=yes
does aside
cooldown 8h
say The crate is yours when both corners settle. | Hands ready under the near face.

rule @mist
when concept=bark here.time=dawn
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Another post appearing in the grey. | The card box stays closed till sunrise.

rule @tea
when concept=bark self.dislikes=cold_tea
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Pour a little less while it's hot. | The cup's been waiting quite long enough.

rule @rain
when concept=bark here.weather=rain
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Look for the first curled corner. | Keep the case away from that wet sill.

dlg @1 resident.hub : The table is dry. I have tested it.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : There's an old place for your elbow, #topic.player#.
dlg @3 resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : I'll keep both sides of this deck in view for the present.
dlg @4 resident.hub [here.time=night] : Just enough light for the red and the black. Sit a moment.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.job=sailor] : #self.trade_words.capitalize#. My share is to see the crate settled before letting its weight go.
dlg @2 resident.job : I have a steady hold and know how much a damp board will bear.
dlg @1 resident.news [world.news] : One card in the hand is showing. #world.news#.
dlg @1 resident.bye : Double back if the lower boards are wet.
graft @curlqueen resident.hub
choice What does that scrap of paper tell you? -> curlqueen
node curlqueen
say It's lifting off the shelf by one corner. The polished wood looks dry, but I wouldn't put good playing cards there for a night.
choice Could you put the paper somewhere else? -> curlqueen_more
choice Return to the dry table. -> hub
node curlqueen_more
say I shall move the case instead. The paper has earned a quiet retirement after giving such inexpensive notice.
choice Return to the dry table. -> hub
choice Leave the cards face down. -> bye
